n. You don't need to be an expert on these practices, but being understanding and flexible if they bring up scheduling needs goes a long way. **5. Ask questions respectfully (when appropriate)** If you are organizing an event and aren't sure about dietary restrictions, it is perfectly fine to ask a broad, inclusive question like, "We are ordering lunch for the team—does anyone have any dietary preferences or restrictions I should know about?" This allows them (and others) to share what they need without feeling singled out. Ultimately, an inclusive environment is built on mutual respect, open-mindedness, and a willingness to see people as individuals. By starting from a place of curiosity and professionalism, you will be well on your way to building a great working relationship.
